# WW4 C++ linting (see AGENTS.md). Applies to C++ files only.
# Disabled checks:
#  - readability-identifier-length: keeps the WW3 variable names (A, K, S, D, ...) for traceability to the Fortran.
#  - bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: inherent to the Fortran call signatures.
#  - cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access: flags std::span::operator[]; spans are used
#    for performance in per-point loops and sizes are guaranteed by the documented @pre contracts.
#  - misc-use-anonymous-namespace, misc-include-cleaner: not meaningful for a single-file library.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -readability-identifier-length,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-avoid-unchecked-container-access,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-magic-numbers,
  -readability-magic-numbers
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: 'model/src/.*'
